    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0601" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12/2¾: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-08T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                                1921—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 5:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>190. Embassy’s telegram dated October 4, 5 p.m.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d433-f1"/>
                    Señor Pani<anchor n="30" xml:id="d433-f2"/> came to see me early today and
                    inquired whether Department intended to make reply to invitation of July last
                    for entering into agreement relative to mixed claims convention. Pani stated
                    that above inquiry will open the road for a resumption of negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
